# #334's OTHER half — a string literal inside an f-string {expression} whose
# text contains a brace. lexer.c copies the string wholesale so its braces are
# text; the frontend's brace collector had no string case and cut at the `}`
# inside the string ("unterminated string", rc 1, where the VM prints a}b).
# The first mirror of #334 covered only the indent-dropping half; this program
# pins the half that waited five months for an enumeration to find it.
print of f"{"a}b"}"
x is "}"
print of f"open{"{"}close"
print of f"{x}{x}"
